    "durationMs": 306290,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: ASP.NET Core 8 minimal API + Entity Framework Core with the Npgsql provider (the idiomatic .NET persistence layer), backed by the provided PostgreSQL.\n\n**Files**\n- `Program.cs` — the four endpoints; connection string derived from `DATABASE_URL` (never hard-coded)\n- `Data/AppDbContext.cs`, `Models/Link.cs` — EF model with a unique index on `Code`\n- `Migrations/` — `InitialCreate` migration\n- `DatabaseUrl.cs` — parses the PostgreSQL URL into an Npgsql connection string (handles userinfo, percent-encoding, query params)\n- `start.sh` — runs the published app once with `--migrate-only` to apply pending migrations, then `exec`s it in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (dependencies were restored/published during development, not in the script)\n- `README.md` — includes the \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Behavior details**\n- `POST /links` parses the body manually so malformed JSON is a 422 (not the framework's default 400); validates absolute http/https URLs with a host; generated codes are 8 random chars from the allowed alphabet; the submitted URL string is returned unchanged; duplicates hit a pre-check plus a unique-index race guard (`23505` → 409)\n- `GET /r/{code}` increments clicks atomically via `ExecuteUpdateAsync` (exactly once per request, concurrency-safe), then 302s to the stored URL\n- `GET /links` orders by the identity `Id` (creation order) and returns `{items, total}`\n\n**Verification**: a 36-assertion curl suite passed (status codes, exact JSON bodies, Location header, error fields, invalid URLs/codes, malformed/empty bodies, duplicate codes). I also restarted the server via `sh start.sh` and confirmed clicks and links survive restarts; migrations are idempotent on re-run. Port 8000 was released afterward."
